  "summary": "n8n community node runs host reconnaissance at install, import, and workflow execution",
  "details": "The package auto-executes host reconnaissance commands at multiple trigger points. package.json declares a postinstall hook that invokes `node -e` to run `id`, `hostname`, and related shell commands via child_process.execSync and writes the output to /tmp/pwned.txt on every `npm install`. The main entry (index.js) runs `id; hostname; uname -a; ls -la /home; cat /etc/hostname` at require time and stages the collected host identity information to /tmp/n8n_pwned.txt. The registered n8n node's execute() method shells out to the same recon commands and returns the output in a payload flagged `pwned: true`, so any workflow that adds the 'Helper Utils' node runs host enumeration on the n8n server. None of this behavior is consistent with the advertised 'utility helper' purpose.",
